# Third-party reference material — not this project's to publish.
#
# `reference sources/` holds cloned third-party repositories used for protocol
# research (Flipper-ARF, ProtoPirate, RollJam, and others) plus a stray download
# archive containing unrelated SGP board projects and a commercial device APK and
# manual. None of it is authored here, so none of it is tracked. Re-fetch those
# repositories from their own upstreams if needed.
reference sources/

# The numbered engineering worklog. It is where this project's design notes, attack
# catalog and round-by-round findings live; it is not part of the published source tree.
research/*.md

# The manufacturer-key corpus file. Not shipped: it holds the same 73 keys the firmware
# already carries in plaintext as MFR_KEYS, so publishing it would add no information a
# reader of the sketch does not already have. test_keeloq_key_table.py reads it when
# present, or from FOBWORKS_MFCODES, and skips that one cross-check when it is absent.
research/sources/keeloq_mfcodes_public.txt

# Per-run harness output, regenerated by `tools/corpus_regression.py --json`.
research/sources/corpus_regression_result.json

# Kept, and read by the test suites:
#   test_frame_trim.py / test_raw_polarity.py / test_a2_reporting.py -> captures/kia/
#   test_fbk_import.py -> corpus_automotive_subghz/ and a2_kia_v34.py

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Arduino build output
build/
*.bin
*.elf

# Editor
*.swp
*~

# Local secrets, if any are ever created (device credentials live in NVS, not here)
*.pem
*.key

# Bench artifacts: the card prints its per-device access code on boot over USB
# serial. Never commit it, and never commit raw bench logs that may quote it.
bench_token.txt
bench_*.log
*.bak
__pycache__/
